{%- comment -%}
  bbi-brand-jsonld — SCHEMA-BRAND-1 (2026-05-29)

  Emits a Brand JSON-LD node for the 6 manufacturer / brand landing pages. Uses
  @type "Brand" to MATCH the PDP emitter (bbi-product-jsonld.liquid:69) so the entity
  declared here is the same Brand hundreds of PDPs reference by name. Emitted ALONGSIDE
  the sitewide chrome (@graph Org + LocalBusiness + WebSite) as its own <script> block.

  Honesty rule (SCHEMA-CRIT-1c): only emit verified fields; omit absent ones entirely
  (no empty strings/nulls/fabricated URLs). NO parentOrganization — Brant Business
  Interiors is an authorized dealer, not the parent of these manufacturers.

  The brands-global-teknion page renders this snippet TWICE (Global + Teknion) — they
  are independent sister companies under common ownership, NOT parent/subsidiary, so
  each is a standalone Brand with its own @id (via id_suffix) and sameAs, no relation
  asserted between them.

  Params:
    brand_name        (required) — Brand.name
    brand_description (required) — Brand.description (plain text, no HTML)
    same_as           (optional) — single verified canonical identity URL
    id_suffix         (optional) — @id fragment; defaults to "brand". Use distinct
                                   values for multiple Brands on one page
                                   (e.g. "brand-global", "brand-teknion").
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Brand",
  "@id": "{{ canonical_url | escape }}#{{ id_suffix | default: 'brand' }}",
  "name": {{ brand_name | json }},
  "description": {{ brand_description | json }},
  "mainEntityOfPage": {{ canonical_url | json }}{% if same_as != blank %},
  "sameAs": [{{ same_as | json }}]{% endif %}
}
</script>
